From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 10:35:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: serialize notification enable

Property requests hold battmgr->lock because firmware requests share a
completion and error field. The notification-enable worker bypasses that
lock and can overlap an early power-supply property request when the PDR
service becomes available. An enable reply can then complete the wrong
waiter and expose an uninitialized property value.

Use the same request lock in the worker. Leave the PDR and response
callbacks nonblocking and preserve service_up semantics. This does not
claim to resolve responses arriving after a request timeout.

Base driver:
https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/tree/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c?h=v7.3-rc5

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -1594,7 +1594,9 @@ static void qcom_battmgr_enable_worker(struct work_struct *work)
 	};
 	int ret;
 
+	mutex_lock(&battmgr->lock);
 	ret = qcom_battmgr_request(battmgr, &req, sizeof(req));
+	mutex_unlock(&battmgr->lock);
 	if (ret)
 		dev_err(battmgr->dev, "failed to request power notifications\n");
 }
